# Carry context on the object

When rendering or handling data that belongs to someone other than the local player (echo kit, village figure), prefer a **throwaway copy with context stamped on it** over an ambient scope (`ThreadLocal` enter/exit) that surrounding code implicitly reads.

- Ambient scopes are invisible at the call site, need `finally` balancing, and fail globally when they leak.
- A field on a copy does not mutate the live fight object for display.
- Concerns with no object to hang on should collapse to the smallest possible thing (one boolean, one call site), not a shared ambient mechanism.

**Name accessors for the question that actually varies.** Prefer `owner()` ("whose item?") over `viewer()` when the reader is always the local player. In base-game-origin code, a latent-bug-style name survives upstream merges better than a mod-flavoured name.
